Article 1 (Establishment and Missions)
(1) An Army Cadet Military School (hereinafter referred to as the "School") shall be established in the Army. <Amended on February 22, 2012.>
(2) The School shall provide the following education and training under the responsibility of the Army and develop the doctrine necessary therefor. <Amended on February 22, 2012; and August 28, 2018.>
1. Entry training for officer candidates and warrant officer candidates under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Military Personnel Management Act;
2. Entry training for persons subject to incorporation into military status as active-duty officers under Article 58 (4) of the Military Service Act;
3. Deleted on August 28, 2018;
